+Import reads one exported JSON array from a file (up to 4 MiB and 1000 records).
+It validates all versions, then imports only the highest-ID version of each key
+into the current project (or explicit global preferences), never into the
+exported scope. Imported IDs, timestamps, and correction links are replaced
+with local ones; expiry is preserved. File sources are verified against files
+in the current project and rebound to it; missing, changed, or escaping files
+reject the entire import, even when their records are historical. Global imports
+accept only source-free preferences. The default conflict policy, `error`,
+rejects the whole batch if any key already exists (including expired or stale
+keys). `--on-conflict skip` leaves existing keys untouched; `replace` creates
+new local corrections. `--dry-run` checks the same input and conflicts without
+writing records, and prints counts of the selected keys as if applied. Successful
+imports print JSON counts (`inserted`, `replaced`, `skipped`, `dry_run`). No model
+or network request is made.
+
 Disabling memory does not delete it; management commands remain available.
